  <section class="section" aria-labelledby="DesignContent">
  <p class="eyebrow">YOUR BRAND. OUR DESIGN SUPPORT.</p>

  <h2 id="DesignContent">
    Big ideas. Blank business card?
    <br />
    <em>Let’s design your introduction.</em>
  </h2>

  <p>
    Need a hand turning your business card ideas into something you are proud
    to share? Whether you have a clear direction or simply know that your
    current card needs a refresh, we can help bring your brand, details, and
    personality together in a professional design.
  </p>

  <p>
    A great business card balances appearance with purpose. It should make
    your business recognisable, keep important information easy to read,
    and give people a clear way to connect. To help us create a design
    that feels like you, we need a few things to get started.
  </p>

  <h3>Your logo and preferred colours.</h3>

  <p>
    Send us your logo in the best quality available. A vector file, such as
    SVG or a suitable PDF, is ideal. If you only have a PNG or JPG, share
    the highest-resolution version you have so we can assess its suitability.
  </p>

  <p>
    Have specific brand colours? Include their colour codes or your brand
    guidelines, if available. You can also share examples of styles you
    like, whether that means clean and minimal, bold and expressive, or
    something more understated.
  </p>

  <h3>The details you want displayed.</h3>

  <p>
    Tell us exactly what should appear on your card or device. This might
    include your name, job title, business name, telephone number, email
    address, website, social handles, and a short tagline.
  </p>

  <p>
    Please send these details as typed text and check the spelling carefully.
    Let us know which information matters most so the design can give it
    the right emphasis without becoming crowded.
  </p>

  <h3>A QR code, or a simpler finish?</h3>

  <p>
    Let us know whether you would like a QR code included. If you do, tell
    us what it should share: a website, portfolio, booking page, or contact
    details encoded directly into the code.
  </p>

  <p>
    For a linked destination, send the exact web address. For directly encoded
    contact information, provide the details you want included. We can help
    position the code so it complements the design while leaving room for
    reliable scanning.
  </p>

  <p class="fine">
    Before printing, carefully review the artwork, confirm every contact
    detail, and test any QR code. A beautiful introduction should lead
    to the right place.
  </p>

  <a class="inline-link" href="mailto:sales@cardistry.co.za">
    Let’s bring your business card to life ↗
  </a>
</section>
